      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\). We start by finding a common denominator for the two fractions.\n\nFirst, let's find the product of the denominators:\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\nThe product of the denominators is \\(34\\), so the common denominator for the two fractions is \\(34\\). Rewriting the expression with a common denominator, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) + (3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{34}.\n\\]\nNext, we expand the numerators:\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 9 + 15i + 15i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i,\n\\]\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 9 - 15i - 15i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\nAdding these two results together, we get:\n\\[\n(-16 + 30i) + (-16 - 30i) = -16 - 16 + 30i - 30i = -32.\n\\]\nSo the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{-32}{34} = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}.\n\\]",
